{"step_index":1459,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:53:37Z","thinking":"**Investigating the Mathematical Conjecture**\n\nSubagent encountered a rate limit while querying an external knowledge source. Shifting focus to independently assess the given mathematical conjecture. Starting a direct analysis using available computational tools, particularly focusing on understanding and dissecting the provided symbolic expression.\n\n\n**Testing Conjecture Validity**\n\nInitial skepticism regarding the conjecture's universal truth arose, prompting a systematic verification approach. Reviewing existing empirical data shows tests for small graphs. The analysis now extends tests to larger connected graphs, focusing initially on graphs with 7 and 8 vertices or potentially specific graph structures that challenge the inequality. Empirical examination of cycles is underway to understand the interplay between radius and Roman domination number.\n\n\n**Analyzing Path Graph Roman Domination**\n\nConsidering path graphs to test the conjecture further. For paths up to length 6, the radius plus one is indeed less than or equal to the Roman domination number. Extending this to P7, this also holds true. Now examining $P_8$, the radius is 4. Attempting to dominate with a weight of 5, the number of vertices covered is insufficient. Examining weight 6 seems plausible.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\"","EndLine":"150","StartLine":"80","toolAction":"\"Viewing HasRadius in GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"View HasRadius definition\""}}]}
{"step_index":1460,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:53:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:53:45+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:53:45+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 80 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n80: \n81: /-- Independence number: the largest independent set. -/\n82: def indepNum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n83:   (((univ.powerset.filter (IsIndependentFinset G)).image Finset.card).max).getD 0\n84: \n85: /-- `s` is a clique: distinct vertices of `s` are pairwise adjacent. -/\n86: def IsCliqueFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n87:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, u ≠ w → G.Adj u w\n88: \n89: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n90:     Decidable (IsCliqueFinset G s) := by\n91:   unfold IsCliqueFinset; infer_instance\n92: \n93: /-- Clique number: the largest clique. -/\n94: def cliqueNum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n95:   (((univ.powerset.filter (IsCliqueFinset G)).image Finset.card).max).getD 0\n96: \n97: /- ── domination family ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n98: \n99: def IsDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n100:   ∀ v : V, v ∈ s ∨ ∃ w ∈ s, G.Adj v w\n101: \n102: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n103:     Decidable (IsDominatingSet G s) := by\n104:   unfold IsDominatingSet; infer_instance\n105: \n106: def dominationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n107:   minCard (IsDominatingSet G)\n108: \n109: def IsIndependentDominatingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Ad\n<truncated 553 bytes>\n────────────────── -/\n121: \n122: /-- Sum of the `k` smallest degrees.\n123: \n124: Stated as a minimum over `k`-element subsets rather than by sorting the degree\n125: sequence: the two agree (a `k`-subset of minimum degree-sum is exactly a choice\n126: of `k` smallest degrees), and this form stays decidable, whereas both\n127: `Multiset.sort` and `Finset.toList` are noncomputable and stall kernel\n128: reduction. -/\n129: def smallestDegreeSum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) : ℕ :=\n130:   (((univ.powersetCard k).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)).min).getD 0\n131: \n132: /-- Sum of the `k` largest degrees (dual of `smallestDegreeSum`). -/\n133: def largestDegreeSum (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ) : ℕ :=\n134:   (((univ.powersetCard k).image (fun s => ∑ v ∈ s, G.degree v)).max).getD 0\n135: \n136: /-- Annihilation number: largest `k` whose `k` smallest degrees sum to `≤ m`. -/\n137: def annihilationNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n138:   maxUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun k => smallestDegreeSum G k ≤ size G)\n139: \n140: /-- Slater number: least `t` with `t +` (sum of the `t` largest degrees) `≥ n`. -/\n141: def slaterNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n142:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V)\n143:     (fun t => Fintype.card V ≤ t + largestDegreeSum G t)\n144: \n145: /- ── bipartite ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n146: \n147: /-- `G` is bipartite: some vertex set has every edge crossing it.\n148: \n149: The specification says `G.Colorable 2`, which quantifies over colourings and has\n150: no `Decidable` instance, so `decide` cannot touch it — leaving `bipartite` a\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"